# {{ product }} — Terraform Helm deployment

Generated from the resolved Kubernetes product using Gearbox templates. This
configuration manages its generated application Helm chart in an existing cluster.
It does not create a cluster, namespace, external database, persistent storage,
runtime credentials or node image store. Establish the selected product adapter's
prerequisites and verify the target identity before using an independent workflow.

Studio export supplies local chart/private values paths by reference in
`local.auto.tfvars.json`; credentials and portraits are not copied into the export.
Keep this directory, local variable files and Terraform state private.

Use one deployment owner at a time. An existing Helm release requires state
reconciliation before Terraform can manage it. Review variables first:

```sh
terraform init -backend=false
terraform validate
# Only in a separately authorized Terraform workflow, after checking ownership:
terraform import helm_release.product <namespace>/<release-name>
terraform plan
```

Gearbox export runs none of these commands. No apply/destroy command is offered
in Studio. The release has `prevent_destroy`; storage retention and logical
backups are separate protections. Host loopback forwarding remains a Studio
capability. Product templates can override this backend via `terraform/helm/*`.
